 ## Background
-The method originates from the VTK (Visualization Toolkit) implementation, specifically in the `VTKMultiVolumeRayCaster` [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address performance issues in multi-volume rendering where dynamic adjustments were needed to maintain interactivity [S1, unofficial]. The concept of time-critical level-of-detail selection is also discussed in the context of volume visualization on large-scale displays, referencing Li et al. [45] [S2, unofficial].
+Dynamic Resolution Adaptation is implemented in the VTKMultiVolumeRayCaster project by Bozorgi [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the issue of performance instability in volume rendering, which can lead to cybersickness in immersive environments [S1, unofficial]. The method is part of a broader family of adaptive sampling and resolution techniques [S3063].
 
